#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Lane D status board (plan §17).

    status --root R --ref REF --ci-results FILE --out DIR
           [--release-tag-glob GLOB] [--push REMOTE] [--include SRC:DEST ...]

Computes every WP's level (L0-L7) and side state, the stage and milestone
state, the decision register, the owner inputs and the §17.3 counters. Every
input is read from REF's tree (`git show REF:path`), never the working tree:
the plan, tests/accept/*, evidence/* and the release tags. GitHub Actions
results come from --ci-results ({"runs": [...]}, see tests/accept/w0c/README).

Writes DIR/docs/plans/STATUS.md and DIR/status/laned_build.json. With
--push REMOTE it commits them (plus any --include files) to branch
laned/build-state on REMOTE, fast-forward only; main is never touched.
Without --release-tag-glob no tag counts as a capability release (no L6).

Ci-only WPs pass L4 automatically (§17.1). L4 for external WPs and an
execution-stage gate need the evidence blob at REF to
have been verified by a green push/accept run (`accept <WP> --evidence F`,
which exports LANED_EVIDENCE=F to the WP's own tests). Invariant coverage
(§17.3) counts only test functions found by AST in
tests/accept/<wp>/**/test_*.py.

    status selftest     # offline check of both rules above
"""

